# Laravel PHP

Controllers and queries stay small and easy to explain in a viva.

## Rules

- Every function and query gets a **3–8 word** comment above it.
- One method = one job. Split validate / save / notify into separate methods.
- Prefer short controller methods that call one model or query helper.
- No service-layer factories or deep folders unless the project already has them.

```php
// ❌ BAD — too much in one method
public function handleDonation(Request $request) {
    // validate, save, notify NGOs, update stats...
}

// ✅ GOOD — one job
// Check donation form fields
private function validateDonation(array $data) { ... }

// Save donation to database
private function saveDonation(array $data) { ... }

// Notify nearby NGOs
private function notifyNearbyNGOs(Donation $donation) { ... }
```

```php
// ❌ BAD — long comment
// This loads every available donation for the NGO city including expired ones filtered later

// ✅ GOOD
// List available food in city
$donations = Donation::where('city', $city)->where('status', 'Available')->get();
```
